I have an OrangePi RV2 with a RISC-V Ky X1 processor.

There are very few application images for RISC-V, so I build them myself.

Look at https://github.com/gechandesu?tab=packages&repo_name=riscv64-containers for built images.

Wishlist:

- [x] Syncthing (https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing)
- [x] Xandikos (https://github.com/jelmer/xandikos)
- [x] WebDAV Server (https://github.com/vaggeliskls/webdav-server)
- [x] Navidrome (https://github.com/navidrome/navidrome)
  Navidrome now has official RISC-V support since (nice!)
- [ ] ArchiveBox
- [ ] Transmission
- [ ] Immich

---

Getting following applications to work on RISC-V is too difficult, so I gave up:

- slskd
- Jellyfin

There are no good alternatives, but I was at least able to create a partial
replacement for slskd — https://github.com/gechandesu/miniseekd/pkgs/container/miniseekd
